## Secret Management for VCS Integration

1. <b>GitHub</b>

To create a secret for connecting to GitHub:

```bash
kubectl create secret generic github-credentials -n argocd \
  --from-literal=type=git \
  --from-literal=url="ssh://git@github.com:22/organization-name" \
  --from-file=sshPrivateKey="$HOME/.ssh/id_rsa"
kubectl label secret github-credentials -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/secret-type=repo-creds
```

2. <b>GitLab</b>

To create a secret for connecting to GitLab:

```bash
kubectl create secret generic gitlab-credentials -n argocd \
  --from-literal=type=git \
  --from-literal=url="ssh://git@gitlab.com:22/organization-name" \
  --from-file=sshPrivateKey="$HOME/.ssh/id_rsa"
kubectl label secret gitlab-credentials -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/secret-type=repo-creds
```

3. <b>Bitbucket</b>

To create a secret for connecting to Bitbucket:

```bash
kubectl create secret generic bitbucket-ssh-credentials -n argocd \
  --from-literal=type=git \
  --from-literal=url="ssh://git@ssh.bitbucket.org:22/organization-name" \
  --from-file=sshPrivateKey="$HOME/.ssh/id_rsa"
kubectl label secret bitbucket-ssh-credentials -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/secret-type=repo-creds
```

Bitbucket Cloud SSH host: `ssh.bitbucket.org`. SSH to `bitbucket.org` is refused after 2026-12-10.

- Add the [Bitbucket host keys](https://bitbucket.org/site/ssh) for `ssh.bitbucket.org` to `argo-cd.configs.ssh.knownHosts`.
- Use `ssh://git@ssh.bitbucket.org:22/...` in `repoURL` of Applications created outside the platform.

Important:

- The label `argocd.argoproj.io/secret-type: repo-creds` is mandatory. Without it, Argo CD ignores the secret.
- Argo CD reads the SSH key only from the `sshPrivateKey` key. See [Repository Credentials](https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/operator-manual/declarative-setup/#repository-credentials).
- `url` is a prefix: the credentials apply to every repository URL that starts with it.
- Use the SSH private key that has access to your GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket repositories.

